## Initial Q&A
### 1. What were Joe Biden's exact public statements about hydraulic fracturing (fracking) during the 2020 presidential primary debates?
Answer: During the 2020 Democratic primary debates, Joe Biden made two notable statements about fracking. In a July 2019 debate, when asked by CNN's Dana Bash whether there would be any place for fossil fuels, including coal and fracking, in a Biden administration, Biden responded: "No, we would – we would work it out. We would make sure it's eliminated and no more subsidies for either one of those, either – any fossil fuel." Later, in a March 2020 debate, Biden stated that he was against "new fracking" when challenged by Sen. Bernie Sanders on climate change. Both remarks required clarification from his campaign, which explained that Biden was referring to his plan to ban oil and gas permits on public land rather than a complete ban on fracking.

Source URL: https://www.cnn.com/2020/10/23/politics/biden-fracking-fact-check/index.html

### 2. What were Joe Biden's exact public statements about hydraulic fracturing (fracking) during the 2020 general election campaign?
